{
  "slug": "research-co-pilot",
  "name": "Research Co Pilot",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "About\nComprehensive research co-pilot for Claude Code and claude.ai — 13 skills covering literature review, methodology, ethics review, data analysis, qualitative coding, brainstorming, manuscript drafting, replication design, grant writing, talk building, citations, survey design, and peer review. A peer collaborator, not a subservient assistant.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills**, **5 agents** and **15 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `citation-formatter` (Format citations and bibliographies in any major academic style — APA 7, MLA 9, Chicago (notes-bibliography and author-date),…), `data-analysis` (End-to-end quantitative data work — cleaning, exploration, statistical testing, modeling, visualization, and reproducible scripting in Python or R), `ethics-committee` (Act as a research ethics committee — stress-test a protocol the way an IRB / REC / HREC…), `grant-writer` (Draft sections of a grant proposal — specific aims / lay summary / significance / innovation / approach…), `literature-review` (Conduct rigorous, fact-checked academic literature reviews), `manuscript-drafter` (Draft long-form manuscript sections — abstract, introduction, related work, methods, results, discussion, limitations, conclusion — from a methodology…), `methodology-advisor` (Advise on quantitative and qualitative research methodology — design, sampling, validity, reliability, measurement, ethics, analysis plan, and —…), `peer-review` (Rigorous academic peer review in the voice of a seasoned professor), and 6 more\n- **Agents** (5): `data-cruncher` (Run heavy quantitative analysis in isolation — fit many model variants, run cross-validation, simulate power, perform sensitivity analyses,…), `manuscript-drafter` (Draft long-form manuscript prose in isolation — full sections (intro / methods / results / discussion / abstract)…), `source-finder` (Find, retrieve, and extract structured information from academic sources at scale), `stats-validator` (Independent second-look on a colleague's quantitative analysis — script + data + report), `transcript-coder` (Process qualitative transcripts and text data at scale — clean and standardize transcripts, apply a given codebook to…)\n- **Commands** (15): `analyze` (Clean, analyze, model, and visualize quantitative data — Python or R, with reproducible scripts), `brainstorm` (Brainstorm and pressure-test research ideas, questions, and angles), `cite` (Format citations and bibliographies in any major academic style; convert between styles; build BibTeX), `code-themes` (Code qualitative transcripts, build codebooks, identify themes, and run NLP-assisted exploration), `draft` (Draft long-form manuscript sections from methodology + analysis outputs), `ethics` (Stress-test a research protocol the way an ethics committee (IRB / REC / HREC) would), `grant` (Draft grant-proposal sections (NSF, NIH, ERC, Wellcome, Horizon Europe, foundations)), `lit-review` (Conduct a rigorous, fact-checked literature review on a topic), and 7 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install research-co-pilot@claude-community` from `Marazii/research-co-pilot`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
